                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07307a12-91de-3042-ab23-429b5e2b0549",
                        "entry_id": "646f5710-1385-3e93-8c20-4e6d1ac50cbe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "rodzaj osady wiejskiego typu na Kaukazie albo w Azji Środkowej"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fcd00454-1e1c-4ddf-9869-c080fbad52c0",
                        "source_entry_id": "646f5710-1385-3e93-8c20-4e6d1ac50cbe",
                        "source_sense_id": "07307a12-91de-3042-ab23-429b5e2b0549",
                        "target_lang_word": "aul",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aul",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c5f6a68-ee5f-35ad-9b01-a5c521db2e83",
                                        "entry_id": "c03a67dc-5738-38e8-9821-49d409a8ac89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A village encampment in the Caucasus, Central Asia or the Southern Urals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b64c8c2-d217-4ffb-a09c-0a65f59d7053",
                                                "sense_id": "2c5f6a68-ee5f-35ad-9b01-a5c521db2e83",
                                                "text": "His sorrel face, his long narrow eyes and dusty boots, where he goes on his travels and what really transpires inside the lonely hide tents Out There, among the auls, out in that wind, these are mysteries they don’t care to enter or touch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "452d3d97-f69e-4413-b324-b17c21ef5789",
                                                "sense_id": "2c5f6a68-ee5f-35ad-9b01-a5c521db2e83",
                                                "text": "Bitter fighting took place for Gimry, the home both of Khadzhi-Murat and Shamil. A highway ran along here, which permitted us to bring up artillery and to subject the aul to preliminary bombardment. We did not fire at any specific target, but if even half of our thirteen hundred shells had landed there, there would have been only a heap of ruins in place of the aul."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bc1b1ea-88c8-4fc1-a663-1161d7a6e742",
                                                "sense_id": "2c5f6a68-ee5f-35ad-9b01-a5c521db2e83",
                                                "text": "Crossing the large plateau, they passed the auls of Megeb and Chokh before reaching Gunib, a significant Avar settlement. […] The Avar auls were surrounded by a virtually uninterrupted circle of mountain ranges and occupied most of the plateaus between the tributaries of the Sulak River: Andi Koysu, Avar Koysu and Kara Koysu."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "aul",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89da9538-6050-36b6-b813-66c8aaa00bc3",
                                        "entry_id": "9504a258-d2a4-310e-9f35-cdc02e4762f1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of auld."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "aul",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26ef909d-2cab-3804-8070-56b2233e6a88",
                                        "entry_id": "c686ce06-a453-394e-9a53-60bf91590b0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Obsolete spelling of awl."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c70ccc1-9608-4e5d-9bb4-02e87f181f76",
                                                "sense_id": "26ef909d-2cab-3804-8070-56b2233e6a88",
                                                "text": "[…] and his master shall bore his ear through with an aul […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "94ee5945-6ff8-4cdf-b6fe-609cc94e1ebe",
                        "source_entry_id": "646f5710-1385-3e93-8c20-4e6d1ac50cbe",
                        "source_sense_id": "07307a12-91de-3042-ab23-429b5e2b0549",
                        "target_lang_word": "aoul",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aoul",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e11857e-f054-3278-8d7a-1f10dae9697c",
                                        "entry_id": "56ae025e-d059-31a7-856e-7fb74dae43f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Village fortifié du Caucase, du Kazakhstan ou d’Asie centrale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b4d26a3-18d3-4c23-aa46-b1aebf6e4dea",
                                                "sense_id": "7e11857e-f054-3278-8d7a-1f10dae9697c",
                                                "text": "Un aoule circassien, foyer de liberté et d'expéditions hardies, placé comme l'aire de l'aigle sur la crête la plus élevée des montagnes environnantes, est un dangereux voisinage pour les buveurs d'eau. Ses habitants, quoique nominalement soumis, n'en profitent pas moins de toutes les occasions pour se livrer à leur haine contre les Russes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a312c8fd-fe23-4415-b6c9-74f7205d0439",
                                                "sense_id": "7e11857e-f054-3278-8d7a-1f10dae9697c",
                                                "text": "L’aoul auquel appartenaient ces grands troupeaux, évalués par Gomboé à dix mille têtes de bétail, comptait environ cent cinquante individus de tout âge et de tout sexe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33b82364-4020-4217-bbdd-9b4b983e39e8",
                                                "sense_id": "7e11857e-f054-3278-8d7a-1f10dae9697c",
                                                "text": "Les grands coups donnés au koumouiss clapotant me réveillent ; dans les six yourtes qui forment notre aoul, les femmes ont déjà trait les juments et barattent vigoureusement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4d43c9a-27df-4200-9e33-371a62c3eace",
                                                "sense_id": "7e11857e-f054-3278-8d7a-1f10dae9697c",
                                                "text": "Ils représentent brillamment l’histoire de notre pays, ses beautés inégalées, la magnificence de ses montagnes vertigineuses, la Caspienne grise, ses aouls, ses villages, ses villes, les hommes qui les habitent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "66f6902e-9e07-43bb-9ae6-421f6083046e",
                        "source_entry_id": "646f5710-1385-3e93-8c20-4e6d1ac50cbe",
                        "source_sense_id": "07307a12-91de-3042-ab23-429b5e2b0549",
                        "target_lang_word": "Aul",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Aul",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f2c95e5-2f51-3b4d-b311-9321bcbd1a19",
                                        "entry_id": "6416a5d8-42f5-3c43-8121-f53ad523adb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Zeltlager oder Dorfsiedlung einiger Turkvölker in Zentralasien und im Kaukasus"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ethnologie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff554fca-de5a-4e34-8f73-372490cb134a",
                                                "sense_id": "6f2c95e5-2f51-3b4d-b311-9321bcbd1a19",
                                                "text": "Er wurde in einem Aul in Dagestan geboren."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "761bf897-180d-49b9-baeb-e42a5a8b2458",
                        "source_entry_id": "646f5710-1385-3e93-8c20-4e6d1ac50cbe",
                        "source_sense_id": "07307a12-91de-3042-ab23-429b5e2b0549",
                        "target_lang_word": "аул",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "аул",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19b191c5-e7d7-38cb-b8ca-33a50bf14d36",
                                        "entry_id": "35d6cc72-4ee8-3631-8589-ca97bdddc32b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "этногр. населённый пункт сельского типа у тюркских и некоторых других народов Средней Азии и Кавказа"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "daac6c69-7043-4e37-85f7-b075e63d798a",
                                                "sense_id": "19b191c5-e7d7-38cb-b8ca-33a50bf14d36",
                                                "text": "Мы пойдём за Кубань и там в спокойной обстановке, в горных станицах и черкесских аулах отдохнём, устроимся и выждем более благоприятных обстоятельств."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d92976f-d27d-46a1-8d1e-cd890f2dcead",
                                                "sense_id": "19b191c5-e7d7-38cb-b8ca-33a50bf14d36",
                                                "text": "При этом имени глаза Казбича засверкали, и он отправился в аул, где жил отец Азамата."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
